    "review": "Pretty good read. There are only a few anecdotes in here that weren’t already well known that will surprise readers. If you are expecting this to be a shocking tell-all, it really isn’t quite that.<br /><br />That said, I think the core takeaway is that the experience of seeing how the sausage is made is never going to be good. Powerful people who make decisions are often overwhelmingly careless and unfeeling. This book reminds me of the very worst of corporate culture that can manifest at any organization irrespective of its size. I don’t know how this will ever change if every company has to show constant growth. The most sociopathic among us will always rise to meet that.<br /><br />I don’t find all of the author’s anecdotes to be completely believable. I saw another reviewer mention that many of her statements read like comebacks you think of in the shower after the argument and it was very true to my experience reading this. A memoir rife with a lot of pointed dialogue, rather than being mainly introspective, can have this effect even if it’s all true, so who’s to say?",
